<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  The audited entitlement set (ADR-026, MACOS_APP_SPEC §8), extended in Phase 5 (ADR-050).
	  Each key is load-bearing:

	  - app-sandbox: on from the first build, so a Mac App Store build stays possible and the
	    app cannot reach anything the user did not grant.
	  - network.client: the Mac dials nothing, but Bonjour advertising is UDP and the client
	    entitlement gates sending. Without it, discovery silently fails.
	  - network.server: the Mac is the listener (ADR-010) and accepts the Android TCP connection.
	  - device.bluetooth (Phase 5, ADR-050): the Mac publishes a Bluetooth Classic HID SDP record
	    and opens outbound L2CAP channels to the phone. The P17 experiment proved the code path
	    unsandboxed; whether the sandboxed combination accepts the classic device role is
	    measured, not assumed. If the sandbox refuses, that is a recorded blocker, not a silent
	    entitlement loosening.

	  Deliberately absent: every com.apple.security.cs.* hardened-runtime exception (nothing here
	  needs JIT or unsigned libraries, and each exception weakens a protection), and
	  keychain-access-groups, which arrives with the Developer ID provisioning profile in Phase 2
	  (ADR-025) rather than being declared before it can be authorized.

	  Keep this file ASCII XML with no BOM and no comments inside a key's value: codesign parses it
	  literally.

	  MEASUREMENT-ONLY variant (P10 luma evidence). Adds a scoped absolute-path write exception for
	  one recording directory so the offline luma measurement can read the received stream. This file
	  is used only for instrumented harness runs; the shipped and acceptance builds use
	  DroidBridge.entitlements unchanged.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.bluetooth</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.absolute-path.read-write</key>
	<array>
		<string>/tmp/droidbridge-measure/</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
